1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,490
In Class 1, everything on your map was on one side, and it was yours.

2
00:00:05,390 --> 00:00:07,651
Today the map gets politics.

3
00:00:08,551 --> 00:00:09,990
These people want your hulk,

4
00:00:10,440 --> 00:00:12,496
and these people will fix your ship.

5
00:00:14,296 --> 00:00:16,375
That's three short records in your file,

6
00:00:16,825 --> 00:00:20,448
and one line that says who is whose enemy.

7
00:00:21,648 --> 00:00:24,818
Here's DS 1 on the Science console, once it's scanned.

8
00:00:25,718 --> 00:00:27,577
Its name is at the top of the read-out,

9
00:00:28,027 --> 00:00:32,700
and the small word at the right of it, t s n, is its side.

10
00:00:34,500 --> 00:00:37,608
That word comes from three lines you read in Lecture 11.

11
00:00:38,508 --> 00:00:40,760
They make a side called t s n,

12
00:00:41,210 --> 00:00:43,004
and they give it a name and a color.

13
00:00:43,904 --> 00:00:45,932
Now look where else that word turns up.

14
00:00:46,832 --> 00:00:48,479
It's on the line for DS 1,

15
00:00:48,929 --> 00:00:50,478
it's on the line for the hulk,

16
00:00:50,928 --> 00:00:52,728
and it's on your tug.

17
00:00:54,528 --> 00:00:58,557
Inside the quote marks, the first word is the side,

18
00:00:59,007 --> 00:01:01,087
and the words after it are roles.

19
00:01:01,987 --> 00:01:05,006
So t s n is the key of your own side.

20
00:01:05,456 --> 00:01:06,870
Hold on to that word.

21
00:01:08,670 --> 00:01:10,538
One more line, further down.

22
00:01:11,438 --> 00:01:14,453
In Lecture 11 this one was marked for Class 2.

23
00:01:15,353 --> 00:01:19,068
It reads a section called sides from your fact sheet,

24
00:01:19,518 --> 00:01:20,959
and you haven't written one yet.

25
00:01:22,159 --> 00:01:23,328
So let's write one.

26
00:01:24,228 --> 00:01:27,038
Sides are records, like everything else in this file.

27
00:01:27,938 --> 00:01:31,281
The section is two hashes, the word Sides,

28
00:01:31,731 --> 00:01:36,217
and a key that has to be exactly that word, in small letters.

29
00:01:37,117 --> 00:01:39,244
Then one record for each side:

30
00:01:39,694 --> 00:01:42,107
three hashes, a name, and a key.

31
00:01:43,907 --> 00:01:45,439
My own side goes first,

32
00:01:45,889 --> 00:01:48,268
and its key is t s n,

33
00:01:48,718 --> 00:01:51,297
because that's the word my ship already carries.

34
00:01:52,197 --> 00:01:55,637
Then a color, which is a hash sign and three characters,

35
00:01:56,087 --> 00:01:58,025
for red, green and blue.

36
00:01:58,925 --> 00:02:01,938
Zero means none of it, and F means all of it.

37
00:02:02,838 --> 00:02:08,886
This one is the blue of that word t s n, beside DS 1's name on Science.

38
00:02:09,786 --> 00:02:12,841
I save, I run lint, and it's clean.

39
00:02:14,041 --> 00:02:16,334
Now the people who aren't me.

40
00:02:17,234 --> 00:02:19,306
Here's where we're going, on Science.

41
00:02:20,206 --> 00:02:24,028
The cutter's name is red, with the word breaker beside it in orange,

42
00:02:24,478 --> 00:02:27,548
and the yard's name is green, with guild beside it.

43
00:02:29,348 --> 00:02:32,847
First the Breakers, with the key breaker, in orange.

44
00:02:33,747 --> 00:02:35,297
And here's the line that matters:

45
00:02:35,747 --> 00:02:37,538
Enemies, and then my key.

46
00:02:39,338 --> 00:02:42,476
Then the Harbor Guild, with the key guild, in green,

47
00:02:42,926 --> 00:02:45,193
and the line Allies, and my key.

48
00:02:46,093 --> 00:02:49,592
What comes after the colon is always a key, never a name.

49
00:02:50,492 --> 00:02:51,911
And I only say it once.

50
00:02:52,811 --> 00:02:55,350
Enemies on the Breakers makes them my enemy,

51
00:02:55,800 --> 00:02:57,042
and it makes me theirs.

52
00:02:57,492 --> 00:03:00,090
I don't go back and write it on my own record.

53
00:03:01,290 --> 00:03:04,603
A side with nothing on it is just a name in a file.

54
00:03:05,503 --> 00:03:08,185
So I give each of them one thing on the map,

55
00:03:08,635 --> 00:03:10,548
and here they are on Helm's map.

56
00:03:11,448 --> 00:03:14,502
The cutter is the grey one, out past the hulk,

57
00:03:14,952 --> 00:03:17,219
grey because Science hasn't scanned it yet.

58
00:03:18,119 --> 00:03:20,758
The yard is the blue one, west of DS 1.

59
00:03:22,558 --> 00:03:25,917
They're landmarks, the way you made the lifeboat in Lecture 10,

60
00:03:26,367 --> 00:03:28,300
one ship and one station.

61
00:03:29,200 --> 00:03:31,965
The Side line takes the side's key.

62
00:03:33,765 --> 00:03:35,118
Now watch where I'm typing.

63
00:03:36,018 --> 00:03:38,172
These two go in the Landmarks section,

64
00:03:38,622 --> 00:03:39,998
above the Sides heading.

65
00:03:40,898 --> 00:03:43,381
If I type a landmark below that heading,

66
00:03:43,831 --> 00:03:46,284
the game reads it as a side called Breaker Cutter,

67
00:03:46,734 --> 00:03:48,728
and it puts no ship anywhere.

68
00:03:49,928 --> 00:03:52,400
Lecture 10 warned you about this next part.

69
00:03:53,300 --> 00:03:56,187
Here's the last step of my story, in the Quest Log:

70
00:03:56,637 --> 00:03:59,848
Bring the Log Home, back to within a thousand of DS 1.

71
00:04:00,748 --> 00:04:04,462
In the file, that step ends with the words reach station.

72
00:04:05,362 --> 00:04:07,932
Station is a role, and every station wears it,

73
00:04:08,382 --> 00:04:10,856
and I've just built a second station.

74
00:04:11,756 --> 00:04:14,683
So the crew could carry the log to the Guild, and win.

75
00:04:16,483 --> 00:04:19,800
The cure is a role that only DS 1 wears.

76
00:04:20,700 --> 00:04:23,216
In the step, I write reach home.

77
00:04:24,116 --> 00:04:26,607
Lint says nothing wears a role called home,

78
00:04:27,057 --> 00:04:29,850
which is true, because I'm only half done.

79
00:04:30,750 --> 00:04:34,622
So I go to line sixty-four, where DS 1 is made.

80
00:04:35,522 --> 00:04:37,950
Inside the quote marks, after station,

81
00:04:38,400 --> 00:04:41,626
I type a comma, a space, and the word home.

82
00:04:42,526 --> 00:04:45,685
The side stays first, and the roles follow it.

83
00:04:46,585 --> 00:04:48,451
And now lint is clean.

84
00:04:49,651 --> 00:04:51,835
Three sides make three pairs.

85
00:04:52,735 --> 00:04:54,654
Me and the Breakers are enemies,

86
00:04:55,104 --> 00:04:57,675
and me and the Guild are allies.

87
00:04:58,575 --> 00:05:01,481
But about the Breakers and the Guild, nobody said a word.

88
00:05:03,281 --> 00:05:06,006
And a pair nobody mentions is nothing to each other.

89
00:05:06,456 --> 00:05:07,585
The game doesn't guess.

90
00:05:08,485 --> 00:05:10,974
Scavengers and harbor pilots aren't strangers,

91
00:05:11,424 --> 00:05:14,612
so I add the Guild's key after mine, with a comma between.

92
00:05:16,412 --> 00:05:18,410
So what does a relation buy you?

93
00:05:19,310 --> 00:05:22,459
An enemy reads as an enemy on Science,

94
00:05:22,909 --> 00:05:26,969
and here on Comms, it's offered Hail, Taunt, and Surrender now.

95
00:05:27,869 --> 00:05:33,436
A friendly station is offered Hail, Build Weapons, Request Priority Docking, and Market,

96
00:05:33,886 --> 00:05:35,729
and it lets you dock.

97
00:05:36,629 --> 00:05:39,243
And here's the one thing it doesn't buy you: a fight.

98
00:05:40,143 --> 00:05:43,164
The cutter has no orders, so it'll just sit there.

99
00:05:44,364 --> 00:05:46,241
Now let's break it on purpose.

100
00:05:47,141 --> 00:05:49,759
I misspell my own key after Enemies,

101
00:05:50,209 --> 00:05:51,321
and lint catches it.

102
00:05:52,221 --> 00:05:55,081
It says that word isn't a side in this mission,

103
00:05:55,531 --> 00:05:57,640
and it lists the keys I did declare.

104
00:05:59,440 --> 00:06:00,257
But watch this one.

105
00:06:01,157 --> 00:06:03,594
I take the Side line off the cutter altogether,

106
00:06:04,044 --> 00:06:05,836
and lint says clean.

107
00:06:06,736 --> 00:06:09,327
And a fourth hash on the Guild's heading is clean as well.

108
00:06:11,127 --> 00:06:13,910
In the game, those two look the same.

109
00:06:14,810 --> 00:06:17,287
Here's the cutter on Science with no Side line.

110
00:06:18,186 --> 00:06:20,419
It reads unknown, for good,

111
00:06:20,869 --> 00:06:23,867
and Queue Scan never finishes on it.

112
00:06:24,767 --> 00:06:27,242
The bar at the bottom counts no threats at all,

113
00:06:27,692 --> 00:06:29,757
and Comms has nothing to say to it.

114
00:06:30,657 --> 00:06:32,586
So when a contact stays unknown,

115
00:06:33,036 --> 00:06:35,278
look for its Side line first,

116
00:06:35,728 --> 00:06:37,781
and then count the hashes on its side.

117
00:06:38,981 --> 00:06:40,516
Here's the yard on Science.

118
00:06:41,416 --> 00:06:43,949
A station in range scans itself,

119
00:06:44,399 --> 00:06:46,599
so I don't even press Queue Scan.

120
00:06:47,499 --> 00:06:50,940
It's green, with the word guild beside it.

121
00:06:51,840 --> 00:06:53,287
On Comms I hail them,

122
00:06:53,737 --> 00:06:57,196
and their answer arrives as a header in the message list.

123
00:06:58,096 --> 00:06:59,677
I click the header to read it.

124
00:07:00,577 --> 00:07:02,369
And Helm can dock.

125
00:07:04,169 --> 00:07:05,385
Now the other one.

126
00:07:06,285 --> 00:07:08,864
It's red, with the word breaker beside it,

127
00:07:09,314 --> 00:07:12,832
and it reads enemy vessel, exercise caution.

128
00:07:13,732 --> 00:07:18,549
I hail it, and it answers with one of the game's own pirate lines.

129
00:07:19,449 --> 00:07:20,732
And then it just sits there,

130
00:07:21,182 --> 00:07:23,575
because being enemies doesn't start a fight.

131
00:07:25,375 --> 00:07:27,856
One last thing: I carry the log to the yard.

132
00:07:28,756 --> 00:07:31,109
The Quest Log still says Active,

133
00:07:31,559 --> 00:07:32,885
because the yard isn't home.

134
00:07:33,785 --> 00:07:36,635
I carry it to DS 1, and we're home.

135
00:07:37,835 --> 00:07:41,188
Now it's your turn: write a faction of your own, with one ship.

136
00:07:42,088 --> 00:07:45,218
Say nothing about it, and Science calls it unknown.

137
00:07:46,118 --> 00:07:48,416
Give it a scan record, and it has a name.

138
00:07:49,316 --> 00:07:51,504
Then make it an enemy, and then a friend,

139
00:07:51,954 --> 00:07:53,559
and watch the name change color.

140
00:07:55,359 --> 00:07:58,173
Next time, we meet the people who fly these ships.
